Troubleshooting Tips
Docker containers not starting:

Check available disk space: df -h
Verify Docker service: sudo systemctl status docker
Check container logs: docker-compose logs [service_name]
API authentication failures:

Verify service is fully started (wait 5-10 minutes after deployment)
Check credentials in configuration files
Test API manually with curl before running scripts
Review firewall rules if using remote connections
Playbooks not executing:

Verify alert severity meets minimum threshold
Check playbook routing logic in orchestrator
Review logs for error messages
Ensure all required Python modules are installed
TheHive case creation fails:

Confirm TheHive is accessible at configured URL
Verify session/authentication is valid
Check TheHive logs: docker-compose logs thehive
Ensure Elasticsearch is running properly
Conclusion
This lab introduced Security Orchestration, Automation, and Response (SOAR) concepts through hands-on implementation. You deployed open-source SOAR tools (TheHive and Cortex), integrated them with Wazuh SIEM, and created automated playbooks for common security incidents. The workflow orchestrator you built demonstrates how modern security operations centers automate repetitive tasks, reduce response times, and improve overall security posture.

Key takeaways:

SOAR platforms reduce manual effort in incident response
Automated playbooks ensure consistent response procedures
Integration between SIEM and case management improves workflow
Proper testing and validation are critical for reliable automation
Continue developing additional playbooks for other incident types and refine your orchestration logic based on your organization's specific security requirements.
